TRIADIC CLOSURE AXIOM (Trifoil knot)
========================================

Let S, I, and D be distinct closure modes.

    S ≠ I
    I ≠ D
    D ≠ S

Define the closure object

    Ω := Cl(S,I,D)

Then:

    Ω ≠ S
    Ω ≠ I
    Ω ≠ D

and

    Ω ≠ {S,I}
    Ω ≠ {I,D}
    Ω ≠ {D,S}

and

    Ω ≠ {S,I,D}

The identity of Ω resides in the
closure relation itself and not in
any constituent mode nor in their
mere aggregation.

The object exists through
irreducible relational closure.
